{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpv-player/mpv/compare/master...e757931859c9e0df7910ef39c1125b191367e060","html_url":"https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/compare/master...e757931859c9e0df7910ef39c1125b191367e060","permalink_url":"https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/compare/mpv-player:fe753a7...mpv-player:e757931","diff_url":"https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/compare/master...e757931859c9e0df7910ef39c1125b191367e060.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/compare/master...e757931859c9e0df7910ef39c1125b191367e060.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"fe753a78246151a2489b472dabcb04f2edd61d50","node_id":"C_kwDOAF6fBNoAKGZlNzUzYTc4MjQ2MTUxYTI0ODliNDcyZGFiY2IwNGYyZWRkNjFkNTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Avi Halachmi (:avih)","email":"avihpit@yahoo.com","date":"2026-11-10T16:46:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"avih","email":"2164962+avih@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-12T19:58:30Z"},"message":"win32: timers: restore perwait behavior on idle\n\nBefore commit 7c65383131, high resolution timers were set only\naccording to the requested timeout using a threshold (\"perwait\"),\nso that high resolution was enabled only for up to 50 ms timeout.\n\nCommit 7c65383131 added unconditional high resolution timers during\nplayback, and switched to that mode (\"playback\") by default.\n\nHowever, it also disabled the per-wait behvior unnecessarily, which\nresulted in much worse short timeout accuracy during idle.\n\nBut the \"playback\" and \"perwait\" modes are not mutually exclusive,\nand in fact completely independent. When both are enabled then high\nresolution is enabled unconditionally during playback, and in idle\nonly per-wait controls the resolution.\n\nThis commit adds a new mode \"perwait+playback\" which enables both,\nand sets it as the default, thus fixing the degraded accuracy.\n\nUsing the following test.js script:\n\n  var t0;\n  setInterval(function() {\n      var t1 = mp.get_time_ms();\n      print(t1 - t0);\n      t0 = t1;\n  }, 16.67);\n\nSince commit 7c65383131, \"mpv --idle --script=test.js\" produced:\n\n[test] 22.283999999999993\n[test] 3.6610000000000015\n[test] 27.578000000000004\n[test] 15.701999999999999\n[test] 16.674000000000008\n[test] 16.75\n[test] 19.789999999999993\n[test] 5.015999999999991\n[test] 26.418000000000036\n[test] 15.665999999999997\n\nLua timers don't ensure accuracy on average, so it's 31ms on average.\n\nNow (and before commit 7c65383131) it produces sequences like this:\n\n[test] 16.78\n[test] 16.679000000000003\n[test] 16.658999999999993\n[test] 16.683999999999999\n[test] 16.658000000000017\n[test] 16.668000000000008\n[test] 16.676999999999965\n[test] 17.307000000000018\n[test] 16.091999999999986\n[test] 16.599000000000048\n\nAnd pretty much the same accuracy in lua timers too.","tree":{"sha":"c3a19896ee38bf4fd4c0271e0a2c20ce3e71589a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpv-player/mpv/git/trees/c3a19896ee38bf4fd4c0271e0a2c20ce3e71589a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpv-player/mpv/git/commits/fe753a78246151a2489b472dabcb04f2edd61d50","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpv-player/mpv/commits/fe753a78246151a2489b472dabcb04f2edd61d50","html_url":"https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/fe753a78246151a2489b472dabcb04f2edd61d50","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mpv-player/mpv/commits/fe753a78246151a2489b472dabcb04f2edd61d50/comments","author":{"login":"avih","id":2164962,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjQ5NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2164962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/avih","html_url":"https://github.com/avih","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avih/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avih/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avih/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/avih/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url"